# Story 17: PTY Resize (30s)
# Hook: Resize panes, resize the terminal -- the PTY adjusts
# Duration: 30s
# Source: story-17-pty-resize.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
PTY resize is automatic. Resize panes freely.

[00:03.0 --> 00:06.0]
Start rysh.

[00:06.0 --> 00:10.0]
Split into two panes with Ctrl+P then n.

[00:10.0 --> 00:14.0]
Type a command in the left pane.

[00:14.0 --> 00:18.0]
Switch to the right pane and type there.

[00:18.0 --> 00:25.0]
Ctrl+L enters layout mode. Use arrow keys to resize. Right grows the active pane, Left shrinks it.

[00:25.0 --> 00:28.0]
Press Escape to exit layout mode. The PTY adjusts automatically -- no restart needed.

